 "note": "The Cluster overview in the Dashboard board's grammar: bands of tiles that each fill the twelve columns - the figures first (host cpu, capacity, fleet, the GPU gate), what is moving (pipelines, temperatures, the control plane, the census, requests), the streams (events, routing, sandboxes, node latency), the estate's composites (Proxmox, Docker, Ollama), the stack and its health, the tables, the stores, queues and lab, the edges (mesh, connections, backups), the terminal. Every tile is a record over a real source: read.map names the envelope's fields (the shape's container <- a path; a dict of things <- rows named by key; every other key <- a field of each row; pick: {label: path} builds a thing from paths anywhere in the answer; keys: [...] keeps only those entries). A composite reads its subject once and its children take $subject.<path> slices, or read on their own; slots share the frame by what each child needs. The page tiles this layout replaced are named hidden at the end. Edit by hand from here.",
